 ("phinehas_pierced_both", "act", "Phinehas rose, took the spear and pierced both, and the plague was stayed — 'and Phinehas son of Eleazar son of Aaron the priest saw, and he rose from the midst of the congregation and took a spear in his hand; and he went after the man of Israel into the alcove and pierced both of them, the man of Israel and the woman through her belly, and the plague was stayed from the children of Israel' (Num 25:7-8; the pair named at 25:14-15: Zimri son of Salu, prince of a father's house of Simeon; Cozbi daughter of Zur) — Phinehas born Exod 6:25, silent until here; Korach's 'from the midst'; the Torah's one spear; the curse-word's skin (the alcove, her belly); AARON'S INCENSE CLAUSE (17:13); Mishnah Sanhedrin 9:6 THE ANSWER SHEET, Sanhedrin 82a-b the limits", 25, 7, 8, "and Phinehas son of Eleazar son of Aaron the priest saw, and he rose from the midst of the congregation and took a spear in his hand", "Num 25:7-8, 25:14-15; Onkelos Num 25:7-8; Exod 6:25; Num 16:21, 17:10-13; Deut 22:24; Ps 106:30; Mishnah Sanhedrin 9:6; Sanhedrin 82a:10-15, 82b:3; Zevachim 101b:10; Avodah Zarah 36b:9; Sifrei Bamidbar 131:2-3", U25, "pinchas", "slain (the DESTROY entry on Zimri, Phinehas the counterparty — 'pierced both of them'), slain (the DESTROY entry on Cozbi, Phinehas the counterparty); Zimri's cohabits entry CLOSED (the act ended by the spear); the plague CLOSED ('and the plague was stayed', the count 24,000 by the parser at 25:9 in the note)", ["saw", "spear", "pierced", "names"]),
